        "created_at": "2026-09-08T16:47:15.665Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Imagine a man half as tall as himself.  Nonsense, right?  It is in terms of atomic matter.  But what if a human being or at least something able to function as one, was not made of atoms?  What if it was made of fractal mathematics, every piece containing the whole, completely defying the conservation of matter and energy?  I think this is how ABSA works, or maybe an enemy for ABSA.</p>",
